@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:durability] artifact-version-immutable
Published versions MUST be immutable and dense per artifact, numbered from one.
A publish MUST create exactly one version, or none on refusal. Replaying the
same originating command MUST return the version it created and MUST NOT create
another.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:durability] artifact-optimistic-base
A publish MUST name the version it was based on. Under the artifact row lock a
base other than the current version MUST be refused with `stale_base_version`
and the current version, leaving every row except the refusal audit unchanged.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:durability] artifact-edits-all-or-none
Edits MUST apply exact, uniquely matching old strings in order. If any edit is
missing or ambiguous the publish MUST be refused with that edit's index and no
edit applied.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity;security] artifact-limits-before-persist
Page, per-publish and per-version file count and byte limits, path
normalization and the media-type allowlist MUST be checked before any blob,
version or file row is written. No per-owner quota exists.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;authorization] artifact-cedar-fresh-decisions
Every read, publish, share, delete, storage and moderation decision MUST call
Cedar with roles read from current grants and current team membership in the
same request. Ticket redemption MUST recheck read authority on every fetch.
Administrator moderation MUST NOT grant content, storage or sharing access.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:audit] artifact-audit-same-transaction
Every artifact mutation MUST write its closed-kind audit row in the transaction
that commits the mutation; refusals MUST be audited in their own transaction
after rollback. Audit rows MUST NOT contain content, storage keys or values,
tickets, paths or tool arguments.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] artifact-storage-namespaces
Personal storage MUST be keyed by artifact and user; shared storage by artifact
only. Only owners and writers MAY write shared storage. Writes MUST be text,
within the key and per-artifact byte caps, and a refused write MUST change
nothing but its audit row.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;authorization] artifact-tool-turn-authority
The agent `artifact` tool MUST act with the authority of the user who prompted
the turn, freshly checked by the server-tool job, and MUST report unreadable
artifacts as `not_found`.
